<title>USA: Sonic Solutions posts Q3 shr loss.</title>
<headline>Sonic Solutions posts Q3 shr loss.</headline>
<dateline>NOVATO, Calif. 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sonic Solutions</p>
<p>Condensed Statements of Operations</p>
<p>(in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					Dec. 31,	    Dec. 31,</p>
<p>				    1996     1995     1996	1995</p>
<p>				    (unaudited)	  (unaudited)</p>
<p> Net revenue		   $4,511  $3,445   $11,614   $11,443</p>
<p> Cost of revenue		2,003   1,651     5,538     5,561</p>
<p>    Gross profit		2,508   1,794     6,076     5,882</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>  Marketing and sales	 1,537   1,611     4,413     4,432</p>
<p>  Research and development  1,472     695     4,180     2,005</p>
<p>  General and administrative  425     362     1,461     1,443</p>
<p>Total operating expenses</p>
<p>				    3,434   2,668    10,054     7,880</p>
<p>    Operating loss	    (926)   (874)   (3,978)   (1,998)</p>
<p> Other income (loss)	    (1)	43	  28	 130</p>
<p>Loss before income taxes</p>
<p>				    (927)   (831)   (3,950)   (1,868)</p>
<p> Benefit for income taxes	 0   (291)	   0     (655)</p>
<p>    Net loss		   ( 927)  ( 540)  ( 3,950)  ( 1,213)</p>
<p>    Net loss per share     (0.12)  (0.07)    (0.52)    (0.16)</p>
<p>Shares used in computing</p>
<p>     net loss per share     7,557   7,466     7,527     7,452</p>
<p>NOTE: Included in cost of revenue for the latest quarter is about $281,000 of inventory write-down related to the discontinuance of a product line. Without the write-down, net loss for the quarter would have been $646,000 or $0.09 a share.</p>
<p>Included in the net loss for the quarter ended December 31, 1995, was a benefit for income taxes of $291,000.  The net loss before the benefit was $831,000.</p>
</text>
